{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"laravel-testing","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Laravel Testing and Pint","description":"Run Pest or PHPUnit tests for everything, a file, the test under the cursor or the last run again, plus Laravel Pint and Larastan.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onStartup"],"permissions":["terminal","workspace.read"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"laravelTesting.all","title":"Run All Tests","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.file","title":"Run Tests in This File","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.atCursor","title":"Run the Test at the Cursor","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.last","title":"Run the Last Test Again","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.filter","title":"Run Tests Matching a Name...","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.stopOnFailure","title":"Run All Tests, Stop on First Failure","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.coverage","title":"Run All Tests with Coverage","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.pintFile","title":"Pint: Format This File","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.pintDirty","title":"Pint: Format Changed Files","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.pintAll","title":"Pint: Format the Whole Project","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.pintCheck","title":"Pint: Check Without Changing","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"},{"command":"laravelTesting.analyse","title":"Larastan: Analyse the Project","category":"Laravel Testing and Pint"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"laravelTesting.atCursor","key":"Ctrl+Alt+T"},{"command":"laravelTesting.last","key":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+T"}],"configuration":{"title":"Laravel Testing and Pint","properties":{"laravelTesting.useSail":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Run tests and Pint through ./vendor/bin/sail."},"laravelTesting.usePestDirectly":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Use vendor/bin/pest instead of php artisan test when the project requires Pest."},"laravelTesting.parallel":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Add --parallel to test runs (needs brianium/paratest)."},"laravelTesting.pintOnSave":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Run Pint on a PHP file every time you save it."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Laravel Testing: run Pest or PHPUnit tests (all, this file, the test under the cursor, the last run again), run Laravel Pint and static analysis.\n// It uses the tool your project has: Pest when composer.json requires it, otherwise php artisan test. Everything runs in the terminal where you can see it.\n\nconst SAFE = /^[A-Za-z0-9_\\\\/.:@=\\- ]+$/;\n\n/** The test that contains `line` (0 based): a Pest it()/test() call or a PHPUnit method, with the class for PHPUnit. */\nfunction testAt(text, line) {\n  const lines = text.split('\\n');\n  let cls = null;\n  for (const l of lines) {\n    const m = /^\\s*(?:final\\s+|abstract\\s+)?class\\s+(\\w+)/.exec(l);\n    if (m) {\n      cls = m[1];\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n  for (let i = Math.min(line, lines.length - 1); i >= 0; i--) {\n    const l = lines[i];\n    let m = /^\\s*(?:it|test)\\(\\s*(['\"])(.+?)\\1/.exec(l);\n    if (m) return { kind: 'pest', name: m[2], line: i };\n    m = /^\\s*public\\s+function\\s+(test\\w+|[a-z]\\w*)\\s*\\(/.exec(l);\n    if (m) {\n      const prev = lines.slice(Math.max(0, i - 4), i).join('\\n');\n      // A method that is not a test ends the search: the cursor is not inside a test.\n      return /^test/.test(m[1]) || /@test\\b|#\\[Test\\]/.test(prev) ? { kind: 'phpunit', name: m[1], cls, line: i } : null;\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\n/** Which test tool the project uses, from composer.json text. */\nfunction detectTool(composerText) {\n  try {\n    const c = JSON.parse(composerText);\n    const all = { ...(c.require || {}), ...(c['require-dev'] || {}) };\n    return {\n      pest: 'pestphp/pest' in all,\n      pint: 'laravel/pint' in all,\n      larastan: 'larastan/larastan' in all || 'nunomaduro/larastan' in all,\n      phpstan: 'phpstan/phpstan' in all,\n      sail: 'laravel/sail' in all,\n      paratest: 'brianium/paratest' in all,\n    };\n  } catch {\n    return { pest: false, pint: false, larastan: false, phpstan: false, sail: false, paratest: false };\n  }\n}\n\n/** The command line. `target` is a file, `filter` a test name. Both are checked before they reach the terminal. */\nfunction testCommand(tool, opts = {}) {\n  const check = (v) => {\n    if (v && !SAFE.test(v)) throw new Error('\"' + v + '\" has characters that are not allowed in a test command.');\n    return v;\n  };\n  const base = opts.sail ? './vendor/bin/sail ' : '';\n  const parts = [base + (tool.pest && opts.direct ? 'vendor/bin/pest' : base ? 'artisan test' : 'php artisan test')];\n  if (opts.target) parts.push(check(opts.target));\n  if (opts.filter) parts.push('--filter=' + JSON.stringify(check(opts.filter)));\n  if (opts.parallel) parts.push('--parallel');\n  if (opts.coverage) parts.push('--coverage');\n  if (opts.stop) parts.push('--stop-on-failure');\n  return parts.join(' ');\n}\n\nfunction pintCommand(opts = {}) {\n  const check = (v) => {\n    if (v && !SAFE.test(v)) throw new Error('\"' + v + '\" has characters that are not allowed in a command.');\n    return v;\n  };\n  const parts = [(opts.sail ? './vendor/bin/sail ' : '') + 'vendor/bin/pint'];\n  if (opts.dirty) parts.push('--dirty');\n  if (opts.test) parts.push('--test');\n  if (opts.target) parts.push(check(opts.target));\n  return parts.join(' ');\n}\n\nconst rel = (root, p) => (p && root && p.toLowerCase().startsWith(root.toLowerCase()) ? p.slice(root.length).replace(/^[\\\\/]+/, '').replace(/\\\\/g, '/') : (p || '').replace(/\\\\/g, '/'));\n\nexports._test = { testAt, detectTool, testCommand, pintCommand, rel };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  let tool = null;\n  const root = () => ferrum.workspace.root;\n  const settingSail = () => ferrum.settings.get('laravelTesting.useSail') === true;\n\n  async function detect() {\n    if (tool) return tool;\n    tool = detectTool('{}');\n    if (!root()) return tool;\n    try {\n      const sep = root().includes('\\\\') ? '\\\\' : '/';\n      tool = detectTool(await ferrum.workspace.readFile(root() + sep + 'composer.json'));\n    } catch {\n      /* no composer.json: the defaults stay */\n    }\n    return tool;\n  }\n\n  async function go(opts, remember = true) {\n    const t = await detect();\n    try {\n      const cmd = testCommand(t, { sail: settingSail(), direct: ferrum.settings.get('laravelTesting.usePestDirectly') === true, parallel: ferrum.settings.get('laravelTesting.parallel') === true, ...opts });\n      if (remember) await ferrum.storage.set('last', opts);\n      await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n    } catch (e) {\n      ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n    }\n  }\n\n  async function activeFile() {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc) {\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a test file first.', 'warn');\n      return null;\n    }\n    return doc;\n  }\n\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.all', () => go({})),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.file', async () => {\n      const doc = await activeFile();\n      if (!doc || !doc.path) return;\n      await go({ target: rel(root(), doc.path) });\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.atCursor', async () => {\n      const doc = await activeFile();\n      if (!doc || !doc.path) return;\n      const hit = testAt(doc.text, doc.selection.start.line);\n      if (!hit) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No test found at the cursor. Put it inside an it(), test() or a test method.', 'warn');\n      await go({ target: rel(root(), doc.path), filter: hit.kind === 'pest' ? hit.name : hit.name });\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.last', async () => {\n      const last = await ferrum.storage.get('last', null);\n      if (!last) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No test run yet.');\n      await go(last, false);\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.filter', async () => {\n      const f = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Run tests whose name contains', placeholder: 'it_creates_a_post' });\n      if (f) await go({ filter: f });\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.stopOnFailure', () => go({ stop: true })),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.coverage', () => go({ coverage: true })),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.pintFile', async () => {\n      const doc = await activeFile();\n      if (!doc || !doc.path) return;\n      try {\n        await ferrum.terminal.run(pintCommand({ sail: settingSail(), target: rel(root(), doc.path) }));\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n      }\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.pintDirty', () => ferrum.terminal.run(pintCommand({ sail: settingSail(), dirty: true }))),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.pintAll', () => ferrum.terminal.run(pintCommand({ sail: settingSail() }))),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.pintCheck', () => ferrum.terminal.run(pintCommand({ sail: settingSail(), test: true }))),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelTesting.analyse', async () => {\n      const t = await detect();\n      if (!t.larastan && !t.phpstan) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Install Larastan first: composer require --dev larastan/larastan', 'warn');\n      await ferrum.terminal.run((settingSail() ? './vendor/bin/sail ' : '') + 'vendor/bin/phpstan analyse --memory-limit=1G');\n    }),\n    ferrum.events.on('save', async (d) => {\n      if (ferrum.settings.get('laravelTesting.pintOnSave') === true && d && /\\.php$/.test(d.path || '') && !/\\.blade\\.php$/.test(d.path)) {\n        try {\n          await ferrum.terminal.run(pintCommand({ sail: settingSail(), target: rel(root(), d.path) }));\n        } catch {\n          /* a path that is not safe is simply not formatted */\n        }\n      }\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Laravel Testing and Pint\n\nRuns in the terminal, so you see the real output.\n\n- **Run the Test at the Cursor** (Ctrl+Alt+T) finds the Pest `it('...')` / `test('...')` call or the PHPUnit method (`test_...`, `#[Test]` or `@test`) above the cursor and runs it with `--filter`.\n- **Run Tests in This File**, **Run All Tests**, **Run Tests Matching a Name...**, **Stop on First Failure**, **Coverage**.\n- **Run the Last Test Again** (Ctrl+Alt+Shift+T) repeats the previous run.\n- **Pint** commands run `vendor/bin/pint` on the file, on changed files (`--dirty`), on everything, or check only (`--test`). Turn on **Pint on save** to format automatically.\n- **Larastan: Analyse the Project** runs `vendor/bin/phpstan analyse` when Larastan or PHPStan is installed.\n\nIt reads composer.json to see whether the project uses Pest. Test names and paths are checked before they are typed into the terminal.\n\nPermissions: terminal and workspace.read.\n"}}}